tests/ir/chain_order.sky:9:5: note: [LA-CHAIN-001] `A @ B @ C @ v` is rewritten to `A @ (B @ (C @ v))`
  |
9 | x = A @ B @ C @ v
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: applied by the checker: the tree-walker and SIR both follow this choice
  = note: A is Matrix[500,500], B is Matrix[500,500], C is Matrix[500,500], v is Vector[500]
  = note: an unparenthesized `@` chain has no fixed association: the compiler picks the cheapest (spec, "Algorithm choice"); write parentheses to force an order
  = note: estimated cost: 500,500,000 flops as written, 1,500,000 flops after the rewrite, about 334x fewer
  = note: not bit-identical to the written form: products in another order round differently, within the error bound of any association (spec, "Algorithm choice")
